<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15198" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">effectĭo</span></b> , ōnis,
			f.
		efficio (only in the philos. lang. of Cicero). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A doing</i>, <i>performing</i>, <i>effecting</i>, <i>practising</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">artis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Fin. 3, 7, 24</span></i>
			: recta (a transl. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατόρθωσις</span>), <i><span class="en">id. ib. 3, 14,
			45</span></i>.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> I. q. causa efficiens, <i>the producing</i>
			or <i>efficient cause</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic.
				Ac. 1, 2, 6</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
